{"id": "EUVD-2026-86631", "enisaUuid": "7c6633f2-ee10-3e85-a5e8-348b89964a70", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btusb: Fix UAF of btusb_data by rx_work\n\nbtusb_close() and btusb_flush() cancel data->rx_work with the\nasynchronous cancel_delayed_work(), so if btusb_rx_work() is already\nrunning on another CPU it keeps running after the cancel returns.\n\nbtusb_disconnect() calls hci_unregister_dev(), which invokes\nbtusb_close(), and then frees the btusb_data. A still running\nbtusb_rx_work() then dereferences the freed data:\n\n\twhile ((skb = skb_dequeue(&data->acl_q)))\n\t\tdata->recv_acl(data->hdev, skb);\n\nUse cancel_delayed_work_sync() instead. In btusb_close() the cancel also\nhas to happen after btusb_stop_traffic(), otherwise an URB completion\nracing with the cancel can requeue the work right after it has been\nwaited for.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc654a72a8d979db15e2773a481e931abaf5a9e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5242050195a711e9cd6a9935f689ab6656b94a91", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/472d005622525b7be155cac99dde2252b0163bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93b59937bda3fffc6386c79f5544a39bc680c8e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa391adb9c755515a89993634745e9079e5ef37c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c12c3117639e78940959d956519c758c57d0849"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mvpx-42x3-8643", "CVE-2026-97977"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "071c5521-a592-3d3d-a845-f0b73f3502b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <fc654a72a8d979db15e2773a481e931abaf5a9e8"}, {"id": "169223c2-8af9-3fd3-b7f3-dfcdc4fb5c60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "27b4c2d0-d42d-3461-8df5-65fc3606f0af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4cc59537-7dbb-30ea-9c80-d57f00ef0f54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <5242050195a711e9cd6a9935f689ab6656b94a91"}, {"id": "596a4057-0f6f-33fa-b0d1-6ece31a0487c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "66840458-d4b0-3703-a5b1-2a4fb5943701", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "7ffee7bc-b7f0-32de-8e6d-84c10d2a5cf7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <93b59937bda3fffc6386c79f5544a39bc680c8e8"}, {"id": "8aed584a-d24a-3f27-97f4-65d9fa6c5bac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "8bccdd65-733b-3a85-bf3b-b33ef6b952a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <1c12c3117639e78940959d956519c758c57d0849"}, {"id": "aa0cb26d-364a-3a81-9fb5-500cfcf0c568", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b249c2d9-39ea-39e7-89f2-a13084017713", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <472d005622525b7be155cac99dde2252b0163bd1"}, {"id": "cd78e305-d157-34c7-9ea7-90ddf9d54e00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "cf6173b4-e183-3485-9883-d2787eca0010", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f22d6af5-328d-3f70-8560-0e3d4a2c45d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "800fe5ec302e1ebbf5e3f891f886deecd49c7132 <fa391adb9c755515a89993634745e9079e5ef37c"}], "enisaI